# Line endings, pinned on purpose.
#
# This repository shipped without this file, and that was a real bug rather
# than a style preference: `lib/client.js` is a *generated* file that embeds
# `src/client.js` verbatim as a string, and `scripts/check.mjs` asserts the
# embed is byte-identical to the source. On a machine with git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default), checkout rewrote every
# LF to CRLF, so the embedded copy no longer matched what the check read from
# `src/client.js` — and a fresh clone failed `npm run check` with
# `lib/client.js is stale` before anyone had edited a line.
#
# The fix is to stop git from translating at all. LF everywhere, on every
# platform, in the repository and in the working tree. Unix line endings are
# what Node, npm and every bundler in this ecosystem expect, and a repository
# that cannot build after `git clone` has no business being public.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only binaries, if any are ever added, must not be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Git's own housekeeping files.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
